{"id": "EUVD-2026-21948", "enisaUuid": "a132f9ad-4ad6-303c-b801-6bd255073c8a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: x_tables: restrict xt_check_match/xt_check_target extensions for NFPROTO_ARP\n\nWeiming Shi says:\n\nxt_match and xt_target structs registered with NFPROTO_UNSPEC can be\nloaded by any protocol family through nft_compat. When such a\nmatch/target sets .hooks to restrict which hooks it may run on, the\nbitmask uses NF_INET_* constants. This is only correct for families\nwhose hook layout matches NF_INET_*: IPv4, IPv6, INET, and bridge\nall share the same five hooks (PRE_ROUTING ... POST_ROUTING).\n\nARP only has three hooks (IN=0, OUT=1, FORWARD=2) with different\nsemantics. Because NF_ARP_OUT == 1 == NF_INET_LOCAL_IN, the .hooks\nvalidation silently passes for the wrong reasons, allowing matches to\nrun on ARP chains where the hook assumptions (e.g. state->in being\nset on input hooks) do not hold. This leads to NULL pointer\ndereferences; xt_devgroup is one concrete example:\n\n Oops: general protection fault, probably for non-canonical address 0xdffffc0000000044: 0000 [#1] SMP KASAN NOPTI\n KASAN: null-ptr-deref in range [0x0000000000000220-0x0000000000000227]\n RIP: 0010:devgroup_mt+0xff/0x350\n Call Trace:\n  <TASK>\n  nft_match_eval (net/netfilter/nft_compat.c:407)\n  nft_do_chain (net/netfilter/nf_tables_core.c:285)\n  nft_do_chain_arp (net/netfilter/nft_chain_filter.c:61)\n  nf_hook_slow (net/netfilter/core.c:623)\n  arp_xmit (net/ipv4/arp.c:666)\n  </TASK>\n Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception in interrupt\n\nFix it by restricting arptables to NFPROTO_ARP extensions only.\nNote that arptables-legacy only supports:\n\n- arpt_CLASSIFY\n- arpt_mangle\n- arpt_MARK\n\nthat provide explicit NFPROTO_ARP match/target declarations.", "datePublished": "2026-04-13T13:40:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:16:06", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80e3c75f71c3ea1e62fcb032382de13e00a68f8b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d9a0af9e43416aa50c0595e15fa01365a1c72c49", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1cd6313c8644bfebbd813a05da9daa21b09dd68c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f00ac65c90ea475719e08d629e2e26c8b4e6999b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7e1b6bcb389c8708003d40613a59ff2496f6b1f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc3e27dd7d76e21106b8f9bbdc31f5da74a89014", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3e79374b03bf9a2f282f0eb1d0ac3776f7e0f28a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d5d488f11776738deab9da336038add95d342d1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-31424"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1086f123-21ea-3168-a3b7-fc6b5422abde", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9291747f118d6404e509747b85ff5f6dfec368d2 <3d5d488f11776738deab9da336038add95d342d1"}, {"id": "219eddc4-b281-34a2-9588-f5b8ba2f545f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.81"}, {"id": "22089846-0d92-37f8-a656-16cf607c6ca7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9291747f118d6404e509747b85ff5f6dfec368d2 <f00ac65c90ea475719e08d629e2e26c8b4e6999b"}, {"id": "294fa4e6-a44c-3bb5-8bb6-3f217c405d54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.39"}, {"id": "3498c8c7-acef-3b6f-a67c-1f6c55f124f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.134"}, {"id": "48b4aa10-af65-37ee-9590-bfcb3adebed6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.253"}, {"id": "4bb51c52-dac3-3034-b42c-80cd1c4c850d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.22"}, {"id": "53a87b41-d06c-3b88-ada3-05395aa9cdb5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9291747f118d6404e509747b85ff5f6dfec368d2 <e7e1b6bcb389c8708003d40613a59ff2496f6b1f"}, {"id": "60737b21-17c1-31ef-83d6-8215a29e4065", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.203"}, {"id": "64d7aa91-b148-3fc9-9afd-25d963faa8cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.12"}, {"id": "6bdd13c3-2543-37d2-b4ac-463dccdcb65c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9291747f118d6404e509747b85ff5f6dfec368d2 <d9a0af9e43416aa50c0595e15fa01365a1c72c49"}, {"id": "71b7adb6-dbdb-36b8-bf72-fd0be2a4cd0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "aecf2105-aa7c-3b62-a2e8-034637d7606b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.168"}, {"id": "b376aa86-9a4c-37b7-80de-bf4bc6f10429", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9291747f118d6404e509747b85ff5f6dfec368d2 <80e3c75f71c3ea1e62fcb032382de13e00a68f8b"}, {"id": "c111cebc-8a05-3c8f-99c2-d851eb7cf4cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9291747f118d6404e509747b85ff5f6dfec368d2 <1cd6313c8644bfebbd813a05da9daa21b09dd68c"}, {"id": "cf8f9e1c-dbf6-3c51-90cf-786cc05dff84", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9291747f118d6404e509747b85ff5f6dfec368d2 <dc3e27dd7d76e21106b8f9bbdc31f5da74a89014"}, {"id": "e2e15079-6568-3d3e-9df3-82b7c1fc6b6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9291747f118d6404e509747b85ff5f6dfec368d2 <3e79374b03bf9a2f282f0eb1d0ac3776f7e0f28a"}, {"id": "f3c61611-d1f8-37af-bb7c-d63fa1fb4276", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1940ae4d-c1a9-3c76-b11b-0d86365febb4", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}